---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<Base
  title="Security · Taz"
  description="How to report a security problem on taz.tn or one of its subdomains."
>
  <header class="section">
    <h1 class="page-title">Security</h1>
    <p class="status">How to report a security problem on this site or one of its subdomains.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose policy">
    <h2>Reporting</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${site.securityEmail}`}>{site.securityEmail}</a> with what you found, where, and the steps
      to reproduce it. I read every report myself and reply within a week.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no PGP key yet. If a report needs encryption, send a short note first and we’ll agree on a channel.
    </p>

    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>taz.tn</code> and its subdomains.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Out of scope:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the services these sites run on (Netlify, GitHub, OVH): report to them directly</li>
      <li>denial of service, load testing, or scanning heavy enough to degrade a site</li>
      <li>social engineering and physical access</li>
      <li>findings with no security impact, such as missing best-practice headers on a subdomain</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Safe harbour</h2>
    <p>
      If you test in good faith and within these rules, I won’t take legal action against you or report you to
      anyone, and I’ll say so if someone else asks. The rules:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>use your own accounts and data; stop and report as soon as you reach someone else’s</li>
      <li>don’t keep, share or change data beyond what shows the problem</li>
      <li>give me 90 days to fix it before you publish, unless we agree otherwise</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What you can expect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>a reply within a week, and news when it’s fixed</li>
      <li>no bounty: this is a personal site</li>
      <li>no hall of fame or thanks page</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="meta">
      Machine-readable: <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">/.well-known/security.txt</a> (RFC 9116)
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy code {
    font-size: 0.84em;
  }
</style>
